    {
      "short": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "body": [
        "<ul class=\"takeaways\">\n          <li><b>SQL</b>: tables, joins and transactions — a safe default.</li>\n          <li><b>Documents</b>: flexible, self-contained records that scale out.</li>\n          <li><b>Key–value</b>: fastest and simplest, lookup by id only.</li>\n          <li>Choose per kind of data; many systems use <b>several</b>.</li>\n          <li>Specialists like <b>search</b> are copies fed from the source of truth.</li>\n        </ul>"
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "next",
        "text": "Next up: <b>Indexes</b> — why the same query can take 2 seconds or 2 milliseconds."
      },
